          "def-euclidean-inner-product",
          "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus",
          "def-em-vacuum-energy-flux"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "pthm-em-linear-superposition": "physical-result",
          "pthm-em-wave-energy-average": "physical-result",
          "pthm-em-plane-wave-maxwell": "physical-result",
          "def-em-plane-wave-definition": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-em-period-average": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-cross-product-in-r3": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-euclidean-inner-product": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-em-vacuum-energy-flux": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let $\\omega>0$ and let $k_1,k_2\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$ satisfy\n$|k_1|=|k_2|=\\omega/c$. For $j=1,2$ let $e_j\\in\\mathbb C^3$ with\n$k_j\\cdot e_j=0$, put $b_j=k_j\\times e_j/\\omega$ and let $(E_j,B_j)$ be the\nplane-wave solutions of [[pthm-em-plane-wave-maxwell]] given by\n[[def-em-plane-wave-definition]]. Let $a_1,a_2\\in\\mathbb R$ and put\n$(E,B):=a_1(E_1,B_1)+a_2(E_2,B_2)$. Write\n$\\hat k_j=k_j/|k_j|$, $T=2\\pi/\\omega$,\n$|z|^2:=z\\cdot\\overline z=\\sum_{\\ell=1}^3|z_\\ell|^2$ for $z\\in\\mathbb C^3$,\nand $\\langle f\\rangle(x):=T^{-1}\\int_0^Tf(x,s)\\,ds$ componentwise.\nThen:\n\n(a) [Superposition] $(E,B)$ is a smooth source-free solution of the vacuum\nMaxwell equations ([[pthm-em-linear-superposition]]), and at each fixed $x$ it\ncan be written with a single phase,\n$$E(x,t)=\\operatorname{Re}(\\alpha(x)\\,e^{i(k_1\\cdot x-\\omega t)}),\\qquad B(x,t)=\\operatorname{Re}(\\beta(x)\\,e^{i(k_1\\cdot x-\\omega t)}),$$\nwhere $\\alpha(x):=a_1e_1+a_2e_2e^{i\\delta(x)}$,\n$\\beta(x):=a_1b_1+a_2b_2e^{i\\delta(x)}$ and\n$\\delta(x):=(k_2-k_1)\\cdot x$; constant relative phases are absorbed in $e_2$.\n\n(b) [Averaged energy density with the coherent cross term] For every $x$,\n$$\\langle u\\rangle(x)=\\frac{\\varepsilon_0}{4}|\\alpha(x)|^2+\\frac{1}{4\\mu_0}|\\beta(x)|^2=\\frac{\\varepsilon_0}{2}\\bigl(a_1^2|e_1|^2+a_2^2|e_2|^2\\bigr)+\\frac{\\varepsilon_0}{2}a_1a_2\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(W(x)\\bigr),$$\nwhere\n$W(x):=\\bigl(e_1\\cdot\\overline e_2+(\\hat k_1\\times e_1)\\cdot(\\hat k_2\\times\\overline e_2)\\bigr)e^{-i\\delta(x)}$.\nThe first two terms are the sum of the averaged energy densities of the two\nwaves ([[pthm-em-wave-energy-average]]); the third is the interference cross\nterm, which may remain nonzero after time averaging at fixed relative phase.\n\n(c) [Averaged flux and momentum; equal wavevectors] (with $u$ the energy\ndensity and $S$ the Poynting vector of [[def-em-vacuum-energy-flux]])\n$\\langle S\\rangle(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\mu_0}\\operatorname{Re}\\bigl(\\alpha(x)\\times\\overline{\\beta(x)}\\bigr)$.\nIn particular, if $k_1=k_2=:k$ then the superposition is the single plane wave\nwith amplitude $a_1e_1+a_2e_2$, and\n$\\langle u\\rangle=\\frac{\\varepsilon_0}{2}|a_1e_1+a_2e_2|^2$,\n$\\langle S\\rangle=\\frac{\\varepsilon_0c}{2}|a_1e_1+a_2e_2|^2\\hat k$\n([[pthm-em-wave-energy-average]]).\n\n(d) [No incoherent or statistical claim] The formulas are deterministic\nidentities for the specified coherent superposition; they are not an ensemble\naverage over phases, and no detection statistics, finite-sample visibility\nestimate or empirical conclusion is drawn. The computation is a conditional\nconsequence of the adopted Maxwell postulate and does not by itself distinguish\nclassical from quantum descriptions of light.",
        "strategy": "Clause (a): $E_j,B_j$ are source-free smooth solutions of the vacuum Maxwell postulate by [[pthm-em-plane-wave-maxwell]](a); the superposition is again such a solution by [[pthm-em-linear-superposition]] (real coefficients). The single-phase rewriting uses $e^{i\\theta_2}=e^{i\\delta(x)}e^{i\\theta_1}$ with $\\theta_j=k_j\\cdot x-\\omega t$ and $\\delta=(k_2-k_1)\\cdot x$. Clauses (b),(c): at each fixed $x$ write $E=\\operatorname{Re}(A e^{-i\\omega t})$, $B=\\operatorname{Re}(D e^{-i\\omega t})$, with $A=\\alpha(x)e^{ik_1\\cdot x}$ and $D=\\beta(x)e^{ik_1\\cdot x}$; the common spatial phase cancels in averages and apply the componentwise averages of [[lem-em-period-average]], $\\langle\\operatorname{Re}(\\alpha e^{-i\\omega t})\\operatorname{Re}(\\beta e^{-i\\omega t})\\rangle=\\frac12\\operatorname{Re}(\\alpha\\overline{\\beta})$ and the cross-product version; substituting into $u$ and $S$ of [[def-em-vacuum-energy-flux]] and using $|k_j|=\\omega/c$, $b_j=k_j\\times e_j/\\omega$ together with the identity $(k\\times u)\\cdot(k\\times v)=|k|^2u\\cdot v$ for $u,v\\perp k$ (from [[lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal]]) gives the displayed cross term with $W$: expanding $|\\alpha|^2$ gives $a_1^2|e_1|^2+a_2^2|e_2|^2+2a_1a_2\\operatorname{Re}(e_1\\cdot\\overline e_2e^{-i\\delta})$, and similarly for $\\beta$. For $k_1=k_2$ the bracket reduces to $2e_1\\cdot\\overline e_2$ and the formulas reduce to the single-wave averages of [[pthm-em-wave-energy-average]] for the amplitude $a_1e_1+a_2e_2$. No ensemble or statistical averaging is performed, which is exactly the content of the scope clause (d).",
        "physical_scope": "Deterministic superposition identities for two same-frequency ideal plane-wave solutions of the smooth source-free vacuum Maxwell branch in a named inertial chart with SI constants: the averaged energy density of the coherent sum with its interference cross term, the averaged Poynting vector, and the equal-wavevector specialization. Excluded: ensembles or random phases, partially coherent and finite sources, detection or sampling statistics, any empirical conclusion, and any claim discriminating classical from quantum descriptions.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Electromagnetism, University of Cambridge Part II Mathematical Tripos lecture notes (2026 author-hosted revision, 236 pp.)",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/electromagnetism/electro.pdf",
              "locator": "§4.3.1 p. 86 (the principle of superposition for linear Maxwell theory: any sum of solutions of the form (4.15)-(4.16) is again a solution, and waves travelling in different directions pass through one another)"
            },
            {
              "title": "David J. Griffiths, Introduction to Electrodynamics, 3rd edition (Prentice Hall, 1999, 596-page retained scan)",
              "url": "https://www.hlevkin.com/hlevkin/90MathPhysBioBooks/Physics/Physics/Electrodynamics/David%20J.%20Griffiths%20-%20Introduction%20to%20Electrodynamics-Prentice%20Hall%20(1999).pdf",
              "locator": "§9.2.2 printed pp. 376-379 (linearity of the wave equation and of Maxwell's equations in vacuum; the polarization vector and monochromatic amplitudes on which the superposition is written)"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "order": 346,
    "id": "em-vacuum-waves-and-polarization-examples",
    "kind": "B",
    "category": "classical-electromagnetism",
    "library": "physics",
    "title": "Vacuum waves and polarization — Examples",
    "companion": "em-vacuum-waves-and-polarization",
    "requires": [
